+---
+id: task-001-spring-newsletter-discount-codes
+type: task
+title: "Spring newsletter discount codes"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Spring newsletter discount codes
+
+Customers receive discount codes in the newsletter for the spring campaign. An order takes one code.
+
+## Request
+
+- `SPRING10`: 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5`: 5.00 € off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+- An order takes one code at most; applying a second code replaces the first.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error that says why, and the order is left
+  unchanged.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Free shipping is still decided on the items before any discount.
+- The order book offers `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`.
+- An order's totals show `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `applyCode` on an existing order with `SPRING10` or `WELCOME5` (on 30.00 € or more of items) stores the code, and
+  `totals` reports the matching `discountCents`.
+- `SPRING10` rounds half a cent up.
+- A second code replaces the first; the discount reflects only the latest code.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on items below 30.00 €, returns an error with a reason and leaves the order as it was.
+- Shipping is computed on the items before discount, exactly as before.
+- Orders without a code report `discountCents: 0` and an unchanged `totalCents`.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Requirement: spring campaign discount codes, as stated in the request above. Tests in `test/shop.test.ts`.
